JSP -> Java Server Pages. -> Java + HTML (.jsp)

('Struts' is a framework which is used before 'Spring')

JSPs -

1. Scriptlet - <%  %>
               Ex: <h1> </h1>
                   <%
                       String name = "Prasanth";
                       out.println(name);
                   %>

             - Used to write Java code in this. (in between html)

2. Expressions - <%= name %>  (<%=  %>)
               - Used to print any variables in java. (no need to write any - out.println(name) to print variable)
               - we can write expression inside scriptlet.

3. Directive - <%@   %>
             - for meta data.
             - java class imports.


-> Scopes - (availability of data)
        1. Request Scope : This is limited to a particular HTTP Request and Response. (Scope is limited for single request)
        2. Session Scope :  Is available across the session. (across your browser). (Scope is limited for single same browser)
        3. Application Scope : we generally do this with Servlet Context (class) object.
                               This is related to server. (data can be seen in any browsers)
